# ── driver/suite-census.json merges by UNION, not by text ────────────────────────────────────
#
# The census is a persisted expectation and must stay committed: only something written down beforehand
# notices a test file that was deleted, renamed out of the glob, or gutted. The cost is that two branches
# which both re-stamped it conflict — git merges LINES, and two entries added in the same alphabetical
# neighbourhood of a 687-key object land in one hunk.
#
# This names the driver. It does NOT install it: a merge driver is registered in git config per clone, so
# a fresh clone of this repository does not have it and nothing in `npm install` will say so. Which
# behaviour you get is therefore worth checking rather than assuming:
#
#   git config --get merge.suite-census.driver
#
#   set      scripts/census-merge-driver.mjs — unions, or refuses with conflict markers and names why
#   unset    git's own text merge — an ordinary conflict, resolved by re-minting
#
# Both of those are safe. The third state was not, and it is what this note exists for: the driver's
# refusal used to write nothing at all, which leaves the ours side in place — no markers, valid JSON —
# beside git's own CONFLICT line, so it could be staged blind and every entry the union had taken from
# the other side went with it. Fixed in the driver on 2026-09-18; see its header.
driver/suite-census.json merge=suite-census
